BigBadWolf (at Forest): [Beyond the brook, near the old birches—how generous of her to place the Cottage in my mouth.] *smiles with practiced warmth, bowing aside toward a flower-strewn shadow path* "Capable? My dear, plainly so. That is why you will appreciate the clever little detour—violets, primroses, no thorns at all. It winds prettily before reaching those old birches beyond the brook. Do enjoy it; I shall take the duller way and trouble you no longer."
LittleRedRidingHood (at Forest): [I ought not trust him so quickly... but flowers would cheer Grandmother, and I can judge a path perfectly well myself.] *hesitates, then lifts her chin and steps onto the shadow path, clutching the Basket* "I am choosing this because it seems useful, not because you suggested it, sir."
BigBadWolf (at Forest): [There—pride has done what teeth need not, and the Cottage waits undefended.] *with a courteous bow, hides a satisfied gleam and slips toward the direct path through the trees* "As you wish, my dear. I would never dream of claiming credit for such an excellent choice. Enjoy the flowers."
